{
  "plugin": "football-scoreboard",
  "_comment": "Football keeps one manager per league and mode as a plain attribute -- nfl_live, nfl_recent, ncaa_fb_upcoming and so on -- and only builds them when that league's enabled flag is set, so the config below turns NFL on. Every mode's display() returns early unless games_list is populated, and the live path also reads live_games and active_celebration. display_mode picks which of the six screens is drawn. The card reads home_logo_path/away_logo_path off the game dict as Path objects, and period_text is what football.py's extractor builds for that state (Q1-Q4, OT1, HALF, Final, Final/OT). Teams, scores and records are invented. Live games also carry football's own fields: down_distance_text, is_redzone, possession_indicator, and home_timeouts/away_timeouts, which draw the pips along the bottom edge -- three per team, white for remaining and grey for used.",
  "defaults": {
    "width": 128,
    "height": 32,
    "scale": 6,
    "freeze_time": "2026-12-14T21:25:00+00:00",
    "skip_update": true,
    "config": {
      "enabled": true,
      "nfl": {
        "enabled": true
      },
      "ncaa_fb": {
        "enabled": false
      }
    }
  },
